    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 84.88 score makes him our clear anchor against the vulnerable arm of Jorge Lopez. With a favorable park factor and a solid matchup, he represents our highest ceiling for counting stats. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier is **Jackson Merrill**, who earns a 70.35 score against Jake Irvin. Beyond the solid projection, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a key situational edge: Irvin\u2019s delivery cadence offers a distinct stolen base opportunity, allowing us to capitalize on our organizational mandate to target speed even in marginal gains. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** both check in near 67.0, leveraging park factors against the southpaw, Joey Cantillo, to overcome the inherent penalty of a same-handed matchup.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day centered on the OF3 slot, where **Henry Bolte** (45.49) barely edged out candidates like **Heliot Ramos** and **Miguel Vargas** for the final spot. While **Henry Bolte** faces the formidable Dylan Cease\u2014a matchup that drags his score down due to the pitcher\u2019s elite skill\u2014his position atop the order provides enough plate appearance volume to warrant the start over the rest of the bench. We are carefully monitoring **Drake Baldwin**; his score of 48.67 is bolstered by his #2 hole placement, but he remains a high-risk play against Jesus Luzardo. We continue to hold **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** on the shelf due to ongoing IL designations, leaving us with less tactical flexibility in the infield than we would prefer. We will keep a close eye on the weather and the final lineup confirmation for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, as any drop to the middle of the order would necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of our daily cap strategy.",
